					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13863732#post-4819746</guid>
				<title>Link to &quot;Top Rated Pages&quot; in sidebar?: Re: Link to &quot;Top Rated Pages&quot; in sidebar?</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13863732/link-to-top-rated-pages-in-sidebar#post-4819746</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2020 07:03:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zyn</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1404533</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>For new readers, a link to the top rated pages of all time seems like a great place to start.</p> <p>Is there a particular reason why there isn't a link to it in the sidebar?</p> </blockquote> <p>I believe the initial decision was made because there was a fairly noticeable bloat in votes and attention going to the articles that had already been popular for years.</p> <p>Many of the highest rated pages on the site are articles written almost a decade ago, which aren't up to the standards expected of current works.</p> <p>If a new reader is insistent on focusing on the highest rated pages on the entirety of the site, they need only scroll down to the archive section of the &quot;Top Rated New Pages&quot; page.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
